From: QuecPi <dev@quectel.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PAL: make DP endpoint configuration failure non-fatal

On QCS6490 with the DP output (PAL_DEVICE_OUT_AUX_DIGITAL), the DP
audio stream could not start: configureDpEndpoint() calls getMIID()
which reads the "getTaggedInfo" mixer control from the AGM service.
That control only contains the HW endpoint tag (c0000004) after the
graph has been opened, but configureDpEndpoint() runs inside
DisplayPort::start() which is invoked before Device::start()/graph
open.  On a fresh session the tag lookup therefore fails with -EINVAL
and the whole stream is aborted with "Endpoint Configuration Failed"
(status -22), so no audio reaches the DisplayPort output.

The DP endpoint payload is only used for the DP channel allocation
custom payload; the graph can still be opened and audio can flow
without it.  Make the failure non-fatal so the stream start proceeds.

Signed-off-by: QuecPi <dev@quectel.com>
---
 device/src/DisplayPortUpstream.cpp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/device/src/DisplayPortUpstream.cpp b/device/src/DisplayPortUpstream.cpp
--- a/device/src/DisplayPortUpstream.cpp
+++ b/device/src/DisplayPortUpstream.cpp
@@ -230,7 +230,6 @@ int DisplayPort::start()
         status = configureDpEndpoint();
         if (status != 0) {
             PAL_ERR(LOG_TAG,"Endpoint Configuration Failed");
-            return status;
         }
     }
